  "body": "What happens: `crates/app/src/posting_serves.rs` `serves()` returns `false` for `Kind::WireEdm` (and `SinkerEdm`) for any post script that is not in the registry. Only the registry's `WIRE_POSTS` (\"Generic ISO Wire EDM\", #533) can post a wire EDM program. A user who writes their own wire dialect cannot use it. This is safe (it refuses), but it is a gap.\n\nExpected: a user script that declares `wireEdm = true` in its manifest (the engine's wire door, #533) is offered for a wire EDM machine, and only for one. A script that does not declare it is still refused.\n\nEvidence: the review of PR #1139 (non-blocking note on `posting_serves.rs:54`).\n\nFound while fixing: the review of #1139 (#533).\n\nEffort: high (safety floor: changes which script may post G-code to an EDM).\n\nDone means: `serves(cps, Kind::WireEdm)` reads the script's manifest `wireEdm` flag. A pinning test shows that a user script declaring `wireEdm` is served on a wire EDM, and that a cutting user script is still refused there by name.\n",
